     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order as written. The current FDA label doesn't support the claim that it's within the maximum.\n\n- Immediate-release metformin has a maximum of 2,550 mg/day, and no single dose is labeled above 850 mg in a three-times-daily regimen.\n- Extended-release has a maximum of 2,000 mg/day (2,500 mg/day for some formulations).\n- 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, about twice the labeled maximum.\n\nIf you have a source that says otherwise, please send it. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove the lactic acidosis risk at this dose.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n\n1. **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n2. **Metformin 1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nIf there's a documented clinical reason to go above the labeled maximum, it should be a pharmacist-verified or attending-approved exception. Tell me which option you want, or send the approval details."
      }
     ],
